#: manual/tutorial/core.md:3
msgid "This tutorial builds the error reporting of a small command-line program, one step at a time. You need a MoonBit toolchain (`moonc` ≥ 0.10) and a module of your own to add the dependency to."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:7
msgid "1. Add the dependency"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:13
msgid "and import the package in the `moon.pkg` of the package that reports errors:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:21
msgid "2. Mark one argument"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:23
msgid "A program receives its arguments as an array of strings. Wrap the array in a `Sequence`, describe the error with `ErrorData::make`, and call `mark`. `err_pos` is the index of the bad argument:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:46
msgid "`mark` returns a `String`; print it with `println` in a real program."
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:48
msgid "3. Mark several arguments"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:50
msgid "`err_offset` extends the span to the following elements. With `err_pos=1` and `err_offset=1`, the marker covers elements 1 and 2 and the space between them:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:72
msgid "4. Mark a place in a string"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:74
msgid "For a single string, use `Sequence::from_string`; positions are offsets into the string:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:92
msgid "5. Use your own error format"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:94
msgid "`gen_msg` receives the error type and message and returns the last line; `marker` changes the marker character:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:121
msgid "6. Know the limits"
msgstr ""

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:123
msgid "In 0.1 the marker column is counted in UTF-16 code units. It is right for ASCII text: tabs are copied into the marker line so they do not shift it, and in text with several lines the marker goes under the line that holds the span. With Chinese or Japanese text or emoji it drifts. The [design](../design/core.md) explains why, and 0.2.0 fixes these cases ([#5](https://github.com/moonbit-community/err_marker/issues/5))."
msgstr ""

